Interop only, off by default: EVERRUNS_INTEROP_ALLOW_PRIVATE_NETWORKS=1 lets
RFC 1918 IPv4 addresses (10/8, 172.16/12, 192.168/16) through the SSRF guard,
because every *.interop.test name resolves to the recording proxy on a private
Docker network. Loopback, link-local, metadata, CGNAT and documentation ranges
stay blocked. Applies to the Company's client metadata / JWKS fetches and to
the personal agent's egress (both use is_blocked_ip after DNS pinning).

